{"id":"h12t3","name":"Frequently Bought Together","lang":"sql","entry":null,"params":[],"limit_s":10,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>The table <b>order_items</b> has the columns <code>order_id</code>, <code>product_id</code> and <code>qty</code>; the same product can appear on several lines of the same order. The table <b>products</b> has the columns <code>product_id</code> and <code>category</code>.</p>\n<p>For a pair of different products <code>(a, b)</code> with <code>a &lt; b</code> (text order), the <b>support</b> is the number of orders that contain both products (an order counts once, whatever the quantities). Only pairs with a support of at least 2 are kept.</p>\n<p>The <b>lift</b> of a pair is <code>support * N / (orders_a * orders_b)</code>, where <code>N</code> is the total number of orders in the table and <code>orders_a</code>, <code>orders_b</code> are the numbers of orders that contain each product. Round it to 2 decimals.</p>\n<p>The pairs are grouped by the category of product <code>a</code>. In each category, rank them by support (highest first), then lift (highest first), then <code>product_a</code>, then <code>product_b</code>, and keep the first 3.</p>\n<p>Your task is to return the columns <code>category</code>, <code>product_a</code>, <code>product_b</code>, <code>support</code>, <code>lift</code> and <code>rnk</code> (1 to 3), sorted by <code>category</code>, then <code>rnk</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p>Table <code>order_items</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>order_id</th><th>product_id</th><th>qty</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>P1</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>P3</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>P3</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>P1</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>P3</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>P4</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>P3</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>P4</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>P1</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>P2</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>P1</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>P2</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>P3</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>P5</td><td>1</td></tr></table></div><p>Table <code>products</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>product_id</th><th>category</th></tr><tr><td>P1</td><td>food</td></tr><tr><td>P2</td><td>food</td></tr><tr><td>P3</td><td>drinks</td></tr><tr><td>P4</td><td>drinks</td></tr><tr><td>P5</td><td>home</td></tr><tr><td>P6</td><td>food</td></tr></table></div><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>category</th><th>product_a</th><th>product_b</th><th>support</th><th>lift</th><th>rnk</th></tr><tr><td>drinks</td><td>P3</td><td>P4</td><td>2</td><td>1.5</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>food</td><td>P1</td><td>P3</td><td>3</td><td>1.13</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>food</td><td>P1</td><td>P2</td><td>2</td><td>1.5</td><td>2</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 10 seconds (psql)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB<br><b>[input]</b> tables <code>order_items</code>, <code>products</code><br><b>[output]</b> the result of one query with exactly the columns <code>category</code>, <code>product_a</code>, <code>product_b</code>, <code>support</code>, <code>lift</code>, <code>rnk</code>, in this order; rows in the order given by the statement</div>","starter":"/* Write your PostgreSQL query here */\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["auto-jointure","paires a < b","doublons dans une commande","division entière","ROW_NUMBER par catégorie"],"minutes":25,"source":"Kata Lab","howto":"<h5>Où écrire</h5><ol><li>Écris dans l'éditeur à droite, fichier <code>query.sql</code>. Efface le commentaire de départ si tu veux.</li><li>Écris <b>une seule requête</b> qui commence par <code>SELECT</code> (ou <code>WITH</code>). Les tables <code>order_items</code>, <code>products</code> existent déjà, remplies avec les données du test : pas de <code>CREATE TABLE</code> ni d'<code>INSERT</code>.</li><li>Le moteur est PostgreSQL. Si tu écris plusieurs requêtes, seul le résultat de la dernière est noté.</li></ol><h5>Ce que tu dois renvoyer</h5><ol><li>Le résultat de ta requête doit avoir <b>exactement 6 colonnes</b>, avec ces noms et dans cet ordre : <code>category</code>, <code>product_a</code>, <code>product_b</code>, <code>support</code>, <code>lift</code>, <code>rnk</code>. Une colonne en plus (une colonne de calcul oubliée), un nom différent ou un autre ordre et le test est faux, même si les valeurs sont justes. Nomme chaque colonne calculée avec <code>AS</code>.</li><li><b>L'ordre des lignes compte</b> : trie exactement comme l'énoncé le demande (<code>ORDER BY</code> à la fin de la requête).</li><li>Valeurs : les nombres sont comparés à 0,000001 près : arrondis seulement là où l'énoncé le demande, et au nombre de décimales demandé.</li></ol><h5>Lancer et vérifier</h5><ol><li>Clique <b>RUN TESTS</b> (ou <code>Ctrl + Entrée</code>) : tes 2 tests visibles tournent.</li><li>Quand c'est bon, tu vois en vert <b>« Tests passed: 2/2. »</b>. Sinon, ouvre le test marqué <b>Wrong answer</b> : compare « Expected return value » et « Your return value », et clique <b>VIEW DIFF</b> pour colorer les cases différentes. <b>Runtime error</b> veut dire que ton code a planté : le message est dans le test.</li><li>Clique <b>SUBMIT</b> : ta note sur 100 compte aussi 8 tests cachés. Soumets dès que quelques tests passent, puis améliore et resoumets : c'est la dernière soumission qui compte.</li></ol>","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"tables":{"order_items":{"columns":[["order_id","INT"],["product_id","TEXT"],["qty","INT"]],"rows":[[1,"P1",1],[1,"P3",2],[1,"P3",1],[2,"P1",1],[2,"P3",1],[2,"P4",1],[3,"P3",1],[3,"P4",3],[4,"P1",1],[4,"P2",1],[5,"P1",2],[5,"P2",1],[5,"P3",1],[6,"P5",1]]},"products":{"columns":[["product_id","TEXT"],["category","TEXT"]],"rows":[["P1","food"],["P2","food"],["P3","drinks"],["P4","drinks"],["P5","home"],["P6","food"]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["category","product_a","product_b","support","lift","rnk"],"rows":[["drinks","P3","P4",2,1.5,1],["food","P1","P3",3,1.13,1],["food","P1","P2",2,1.5,2]]}},{"input":{"tables":{"order_items":{"columns":[["order_id","INT"],["product_id","TEXT"],["qty","INT"]],"rows":[[1,"P5",1],[1,"P6",1],[2,"P5",1],[2,"P6",1],[3,"P2",1]]},"products":{"columns":[["product_id","TEXT"],["category","TEXT"]],"rows":[["P1","food"],["P2","food"],["P3","drinks"],["P4","drinks"],["P5","home"],["P6","food"]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["category","product_a","product_b","support","lift","rnk"],"rows":[["home","P5","P6",2,1.5,1]]}}],"hidden_n":8,"hidden":"","solution":""}